      en: "Ashuganj Power Station is a large gas-fired power plant in Chittagong Division, near the town of Ashuganj. Commissioned in 1978, its initial capacity was 120 MW. After multiple expansions, the installed capacity now stands at about 580 MW. The plant comprises steam and gas turbine units. It is operated by the Bangladesh Power Development Board (BPDB) and feeds into the national grid. Fuel is supplied from nearby gas fields. Recent upgrades have improved efficiency and reduced emissions. The station is critical for electricity supply in eastern Bangladesh. Due to aging infrastructure, gradual decommissioning or retrofitting is planned.",
